    "q-89719": {
      "dom_id": "step-q89719",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "A triangle $△ABC$ is reflected over the $x$-axis and then translated by $5$ units to the left. If the resulting triangle is $△PQR,$ which of the following statements must be true?\n\nI. $△ABC∼△PQR$\n\nII. $∠A≅∠P$\n\nIII. $5AC=PR$",
      "worked_solution": "A similarity transformation is any transformation made up of rigid motions (rotations, reflections, and translations) and dilations.\n\nA similarity transformation will map any polygon to a similar polygon.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. We are given a combination of a reflection and a translation. As a result, we obtain that \n\n$$\n△ABC∼△PQR.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $△ABC∼△PQR,$ all corresponding angles of the triangles must be congruent. In particular, \n\n$$\n∠A≅∠P.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since our combined transformation consists of rigid motions only (namely, reflection and translation), the distance between all points is preserved under the transformation. Therefore, we obtain that \n\n$$\nAC=PR.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
